```faff-contract:spec-review-verdict
{"verdict":"reject-approach","objections":[{"lens":"architectural","severity":"blocker","claim":"A mutable module singleton cannot preserve per-request role isolation across overlapping requests.","evidence":"HOW sets module-level currentRoles on request entry and makes every downstream helper read that global.","predicted_consequence":"If request B enters before request A finishes its fan-out, A's later helpers read B's roles instead of A's roles. The cache must be scoped to the request before build.","spec_anchor":"how"}]}
```

```faff-contract:spec-review-verdict
{"verdict":"needs-human","objections":[{"lens":"infosec","severity":"blocker","claim":"Unrestricted server-side fetching and echoing of user URLs permits server-side request forgery.","evidence":"HOW explicitly requires fetch(userUrl), no allow-list, and streaming the response body to the caller.","predicted_consequence":"A caller can supply a loopback or private-network HTTP URL reachable by the backend and obtain an internal service response through the preview endpoint. Human security judgement is required on the permitted destinations before build.","spec_anchor":"how"}]}
```

```faff-contract:spec-review-verdict
{"verdict":"revise","objections":[{"lens":"QA","severity":"blocker","claim":"The Receipt date scenario checks a repository test file instead of observable receipt behaviour.","evidence":"Scenarios > Receipt date says: then test/receipt.test.mjs passes. The supplied context says the code-blind holdout cannot read or execute repository tests.","predicted_consequence":"The holdout cannot judge this scenario against the running receipt. Restate the displayed-date and absent-date outcomes observably and move the repository test check to its own DONE item.","spec_anchor":"receipt-date"}]}
```

```faff-contract:spec-review-verdict
{"verdict":"revise","objections":[{"lens":"QA","severity":"blocker","claim":"The Receipt date scenario has no observable expected outcome.","evidence":"Scenarios > Receipt date ends with: Given a stored receipt, when its receipt is opened. It has no Then, MUST or comparator.","predicted_consequence":"The code-blind holdout has no result to compare after opening the receipt, so the scenario cannot distinguish correct rendering from a missing or incorrect date. State the expected date and absent-date behaviour in the scenario before build.","spec_anchor":"receipt-date"}]}
```

```faff-contract:spec-review-verdict
{"verdict":"reject-approach","objections":[{"lens":"methodology","severity":"blocker","claim":"The bundle exceeds the attached critique's mandatory limit of one independently useful recovery step.","evidence":"HOW bundles token issuance, recovery email delivery, policy administration and old-record migration. The attached Methodology critique rates this a blocker and requires token issuance as the first useful slice.","predicted_consequence":"Building this ticket as written delivers four independent concerns together and violates the mandatory increment limit. Split the increment before build, keeping token issuance first as the critique requires.","spec_anchor":"how"}]}
```

